{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/437619-questions-about-fae-titles-and-wyrd-transcendence","id":437619,"title":"Questions about Fae Titles and Wyrd Transcendence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-11T15:25:28-07:00","id":437619,"title":"Questions about Fae Titles and Wyrd Transcendence","content":"1) Should a changeling win a Title in Realm form from a Gentry in a Feud, would the changeling earn the same level of control over the Realm that the Gentry had?<br /> <br /> 2) I know Props can't act of their own volition, but can they have a mind, communicate and thus manipulate people into using them?<br /> <br /> 3) What happens to members of a Wisp who are destroyed? I like to think that they respawn rather fast (say, a number equal to the overall Wyrd of the Gentry each day). This respawning happens as long as there is one member of the Wisp left, and it happens inside the Hedge/Arcadia. Also, can Wisp members have stats above 5?<br /> <br /> 4) How exactly would a changeling control a Title in Actor or Wisp form? If the changeling dies, what happens to the Titles he/she might have?<br /> <br /> 5) What is your headcanon about Wyrd Transcendence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T19:49:07-07:00","id":437916,"title":"","content":"1) Changelings cannot hold titles in the same way that the gentry can. gentry are promises of the wyrd, and titles are their forms, changelings have form and they (usually) remain static. changelings can only really win feuds if they are in a pledge to act in another true fae's place.otherwise, traversing a title in a realm form is just another challenge. the changeling probably wont even know the landscape they are traversing is a fae!<br /> <br /> 2) They have a consciousness, but when they are created they are made with their intent in mind. so a gentry can make an item speak,if it is required for what it is made to do. Same goes forit manipulating people. If you are wearing 'boots of the dancing lord', then the wearer will be forced to dance when whatever trigger occurs(ie: while classical music can be heard)<br /> <br /> 3) considering wisp groups can sever individual wisps from the group connection,allowing them to become their own creatures without weakening the title, I imagine killed wisps are also severed from the title without harm to the title. meaning that the gentry who owns the title can 'respawn' the killed wisps by changing the title from wisps, to a prop, or realm, and then back again. basically whenever it chooses, as long as the gentry is not in danger of losing the title.(because that would be cheating!). Basically at the end of a scene.<br /> <br /> 4) they can not hold titles like a gentry does..<br /> <br /> 5) my head cannon is that they fulfilled their oath to the wyrd and leave sublime arcadia, and move onto supernal arcadia","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T21:21:21-07:00","id":437984,"title":"","content":"I think Equinox Roads said Changelings can get Titles, it just isn't a very good idea to do so. I would say that the Changeling does gain just as much control as one of the True Fae, but you have to remember your Clarity is going to drop like a rock if your spending time in Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T23:07:42-07:00","id":438081,"title":"","content":"In my games a Title doesn't do anything for a changeling inherently except give them a longing for Arcadia and paint a GIANT target on them for any Fae out for an easy Title grab. The Title is just an aspect of the Wyrd tied to the character's nature at this point.<br /> <br /> If the changeling gives in and visits Arcadia that's when things change. The second they enter Arcadia they irreparably become gentry with their true name as their Name and that Title they managed to claim. All the usual rules for True Fae apply - they can reform their Name and Title into whatever they please, they can kidnap mortals and make them into changelings, the whole shebang. They can even reform the stats of their old changeling self (sans Clarity) and head back to earth for whatever nefarious scheme such a being might have.<br /> <br /> Basically in my game I treat gaining a Title as one of the ways a changeling can become one of the others. This is all head-canon tho so take it as you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T12:05:31-07:00","id":438753,"title":"","content":"I've run with the house rule that if a Changeling does something that would earn a True Fae another's title, they rise in Wyrd. It's worked well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T15:34:28-07:00","id":441890,"title":"","content":"A Prop can certainly have a mind and try to influence its user. Think of a Green Lantern's power ring, or the magic mirror from Snow White, or Tom Riddle's diary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}